s, you know that taking the first animations out of your videos can be a pain to have something clean on the first passes.\n>\n> Take a movement that exists on a video and having it directly inside the game engine is what Unreal Epic Games' team of magicians solves.\n>\n> In this showcase: a four second attack animation from a gameplay video on YouTube, 1080p 30 fps up to 2160p 60 fps for better results at the cost of longer waiting time, running locally on any machine. The point of the write up is running it on macOS, which is not supported natively. The plugin is still experimental, and I did not experience any bug running it 24/24 for around 16 more custom animations.\n>\n> No suit, no studio, no actor. Just the video.\n>\n> The diagnosis is the part worth sharing, because it applies well beyond this plugin:\n>\n> **1.** Eliminate the obvious suspect first. Everyone assumes Windows only, so I checked. The plugin declares no platform allowlist, and it already ships universal arm64 binaries. A plugin Epic never built for macOS does not ship macOS binaries.\n>\n> **2.** Read what the error actually says. It offers two possibilities, missing or built with a different engine version. Only the second was plausible. The plugin announced build 54595663, the engine expected 55116800.\n>\n> **3.** Understand why the obvious fix fails. A Launcher engine is an Installed Build, and Epic deliberately blocks recompilation of anything inside the engine folder.\n>\n> **4.** Look for the asymmetry. An engine plugin cannot be recompiled there, but a project plugin can. So the plugin does not need to be rebuilt where it sits, it needs to sit where rebuilding is allowed. 63 seconds, 103 compile units, and it loads.\n>\n> That fourth question is the one that pays, and it is the one nobody asks.\n>\n> The full protocol, the scripts and the traps are public, and free:\n>\n> Article: https://matthieuhuguet.com/reels/metahuman-markerless-macos\n> Repo: https://github.com/matthieuhuguet/MetaHuman-Animator-Markerless-Motion-Capture-Plugin-macOS\n>\n> The plugin belongs to Epic Games. My contribution is narrow and I would rather state it plainly: I compiled it on macOS and ran it end to end until an animation came out. Thanks to their teams for the work.\n>\n> #UnrealEngine #MetaHuman #MotionCapture #TechnicalArt #GameDevelopment #macOS\n\n---\n\nUn détail sur Instagram : les liens n'y sont pas cliquables dans la légende, d'où la mention de la bio. Sur LinkedIn ils le sont, mais la plateforme réduit la portée des posts contenant des liens externes ; si tu veux maximiser la diffusion, mets-les en premier commentaire plutôt que dans le corps."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_read_input_tokens":551028,"output_tokens":1650,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1650,"cache_read_input_tokens":551028,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1242,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1242},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeJD6oA8wXQSb88JiLMNU","type":"assistant","uuid":"5ec7e2cb-4f7e-4e53-a7be-1d58e18726b0","timestamp":"2026-08-22T17:50:03.340Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"ee0a6edb-af5c-440a-a832-13607f27c7be","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"main","slug":"rosy-wobbling-squid"}
